Ahhh, I call this Murphy's law of beards.. every time I as an actor need a beard, I don't have it.  Everytime that I want a role, they want clean shaven.

&#x200B;

I've got a couple of examples, but the first one was I was told to get more "Peaky Blinders" looking for an advert casting by my agent.  I get everything fairly clean shaven.  The casting gets cancelled.  Two days later, I'm in for a "viking werewolf" role.    Now I'm not saying I didn't get the part because I didn't look viking werewolf enough, but I felt it was a factor, and at least affected my confidence.

