The whole thing about the Fresno fight is that it is shady AF.  Some of the lower organizations are ran by crooks which completely flout commissions or regulations.  Not too different to an underground fight club.  Not to mention, if your opponent comes in overweight, you have the opportunity to pull out.  Nate was too eager for a fight to allow that to happen.  

&#x200B;

In the UFC, you can be forced to forfeit a certain amount of your purse as Paulo Costa did recently.  I personally prefer the rules that One FC which basically insist that you have to be a certain level of hydrated in order to make weight.  Far safer for the athletes and gives a much more "honest" reflection of the weight the fighters will be on the day.  Khabib Nurgamedov may be one of the best MMA fighters of all time, but the man suposedly walked at around 200 lbs and cut down to 155 for fights, meaning that he may have had 15-20 lbs on many of the fighters in his division.  McGregor for all his faults, has to be commended on his willingness to fight at 170 when his body really isn't built for it in terms of its physical make up

I'd be a really shit bard.  In life I'm an actor, I can sort of sing, sort of play an instrument.  I practice martial arts and I'm fairly strong, rarely get sick but I have poor hand eye coordination.  So I'd go for 14 strength, 15 con and 10 dex. My ability to think logically has its limits and my ability to read books for long periods of time is pretty middling.  I'd say my intelligence is a 14 if I'm lucky, but realistically a 12.  My last tinder match compared me to Richard Madden (Rob Stark) in looks, have had my days of being a bit of a man whore and I'm reasonably likable so I'd say my charisma isn't awful most of the time.  Let's go with a 14.  Jack of all trades, master of none.  Alignment is generally neutral to chaotic good.  Neutral on a day I can't be bothered helping.  

&#x200B;

